        subsection "Touch Control Modes"

            text
                Bedrock supports multiple touchscreen control schemes. Available layouts can depend on the device and current version.

                Touch control settings can be found in Minecraft's Controls settings.
            end

        end

    end

    section "Changing Controls"

        subsection "Keyboard And Mouse"

            text
                To change keyboard and mouse controls, open Minecraft Settings and open the Keyboard and Mouse controls section.

                Select the action you want to change and assign a different key or mouse input.
            end

        end

        subsection "Controller"

            text
                To change controller controls, open Minecraft Settings and open the Controller controls section.

                Available controller options depend on the platform and current Bedrock version.
            end

        end

        subsection "Touch"

            text
                Touchscreen controls are configured through the Touch controls settings.

                Different touch control schemes may provide different layouts and interaction methods.
            end

        end

        subsection "Resetting Controls"

            text
                Minecraft provides an option to restore controls to their default settings.

                Resetting controls is useful if custom bindings become confusing or stop matching the controls listed in this guide.
            end

        end

    end

    section "Control Categories"

        text
            Minecraft controls can generally be organized into movement, camera, combat, block interaction, item management, inventory, hotbar selection, chat, commands, menus, multiplayer, and creative-mode controls.

            Keyboard and mouse players have the largest set of directly assignable physical inputs. Controller players use buttons, triggers, bumpers, sticks, and directional buttons. Touchscreen players use configurable virtual controls.
        end

    end

    section "Important Notes"

        note
            Default controls can differ between platforms.
        end

        note
            Controls can change between Minecraft versions.
        end

        note
            A customized control takes priority over the default control listed in this guide.
        end

        note
            Some actions only appear when the feature that uses them is available.
        end

        note
            Touchscreen layouts are different from keyboard and mouse key bindings and cannot be represented as a normal keyboard key list.
        end

    end

end